cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use holom-core in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "holom-core: Numerical Diffraction, Computer-Generated Holography, and Reproducible Legacy Audit in Python and PyTorch"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dudbilopr/holom-core"
url: "https://github.com/dudbilopr/holom-core"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pabón Riaño"
    given-names: "Dudbil Olvasada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7239-3497"
    email: "dpabon180@unab.edu.co"
    affiliation: "Universidad Autónoma de Bucaramanga (UNAB)"
keywords:
  - digital holography
  - computer-generated holography
  - fresnel diffraction
  - angular spectrum
  - zero-order suppression
  - autofocus
  - gpu acceleration
  - pytorch
abstract: >
  holom-core is a verified Python and PyTorch library implementing scalar
  diffraction propagators (single-FFT Fresnel, convolution-based Fresnel, and
  angular spectrum), classic and iterative computer-generated hologram (CGH)
  encodings, zero-order suppression filters, multi-plane depth-from-focus, and
  an automated numerical audit of legacy MATLAB digital holography codes
  developed in 2012-2015.
